Subject: [PATCH] arm64: package the uncompressed Image

The builder compiles the kernel with an explicit target, so for arm64
KERNEL_IMAGE_TYPE=Image and arch/arm64/boot/Image is what gets built.
scripts/package/builddeb, however, copies "$(make image_name)", and
image_name expands to $(notdir $(KBUILD_IMAGE)), i.e. Image.gz, which was
never produced. Packaging then dies with

  cp: cannot stat 'arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz': No such file or directory
  make[4]: *** [scripts/Makefile.package:90: intdeb-pkg] Error 1

so no linux-image-*.deb is produced and the image build stops at the
"Installation of linux-image-... failed" step.

Point KBUILD_IMAGE at the uncompressed Image for the non-EFI case, which is
what the sunxi boot scripts load anyway (boot-sun50iw9-next.cmd does
"load ${devtype} ${devnum} ${kernel_addr_r} ${prefix}Image").

This is the same change the vendor already carries unused in
external/patch/misc/general-packaging-5.6.y.patch, reduced to the single
hunk that matters here; that file also rewrites builddeb/mkdebian for
kernel 5.6.y and does not apply to the 6.1.y tree used by sun50iw9/next.

--- a/arch/arm64/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/Makefile
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@ boot		:= arch/arm64/boot
 
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_EFI_ZBOOT),)
-KBUILD_IMAGE	:= $(boot)/Image.gz
+KBUILD_IMAGE	:= $(boot)/Image
 else
 KBUILD_IMAGE	:= $(boot)/vmlinuz.efi
 endif
